# Docker build context for the backend images, which are all built from the
# repo root (see <service>/Dockerfile). Without this file the daemon receives
# the whole working tree on every build — 4.06 GB here, almost all of it
# node_modules, target/ and the Angular dist — for images whose payload is a
# few tens of MB. The build only needs the poms, each module's src/, and
# config-repo/.
#
# Only the context root's .dockerignore is honoured: BuildKit reads the file at
# the root of the context and nowhere else, so the per-module copies are inert
# unless a module is ever built with itself as the context.

# Build output and dependencies: never inputs to a build.
**/node_modules
**/target
**/dist
**/.angular

# VCS and editor state.
**/.git
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# The frontend is built and deployed by Vercel, not by any of these images.
ecom-frontend/

# Documentation and notes are not on any classpath.
docs/
*.md

# Root-level Node tooling (seed-data.js/ts and their lockfiles) belongs to the
# local seeding workflow, not to a service image.
node_modules/
src/
.gitignore

# Keycloak's realm export is mounted by docker-compose for local dev and copied
# into the image by keycloak-deploy/Dockerfile, which uses that directory as its
# own context — neither path reads it from this one.
keycloak/
